      ⍝ regression (plan.txt, 2026-09-05): )LOAD/)COPY of a .xml file
      ⍝ whose trailing 4 NUL bytes (written by )SAVE "so that string
      ⍝ functions can be used if the file should be mmap()ed") are
      ⍝ missing -- e.g. a corrupted or truncated file -- used to be
      ⍝ handled ad-hoc, one call site at a time, by a family of
      ⍝ specially-bounded bounded_strstr()/bounded_strtoll()/
      ⍝ bounded_strtod() helpers. Replaced by a single up-front check
      ⍝ (has_trailing_NUL(), Archive.hh) in both read_Workspace() and
      ⍝ check_checksum(): every ordinary (unbounded) libc-style scan used
      ⍝ elsewhere in the reader can then safely assume a real NUL exists
      ⍝ within the mapped file. A file failing that check is refused
      ⍝ cleanly instead of being parsed at all.
      ⍝
      ⍝ note: like the checksum-mismatch WARNING above, the "is corrupt
      ⍝ or truncated" message itself goes to plain CERR and is not part
      ⍝ of the reference comparison -- verify the safe-refusal behavior
      ⍝ instead: TRUNCTEST must still be undefined afterwards, proving
      ⍝ )LOAD returned early rather than crashing or partially loading.
      ⍝
      )CLEAR
CLEAR WS

      )WSID trunc_test
WAS CLEAR WS

      TRUNCTEST←42
      )SAVE trunc_test
20⁰-⁰-⁰  ⁰:⁰:⁰ (GMT⁵⁰) 

      data ← ⎕FIO[26] 'testcases/libroot/workspaces/trunc_test.xml'
      new_data ← ¯5↓data
      Handle ← 'w' ⎕FIO[3] 'testcases/libroot/workspaces/trunc_test.xml'
      Wcount ← (⎕UCS new_data) ⎕FIO[7] Handle

      ⎕FIO[4] Handle
0

      )LOAD trunc_test
      ⎕NC 'TRUNCTEST'
0

      )DROP trunc_test.xml
³

      ⍝ Bugs28 #29 regression: a derived function with a value/lambda
      ⍝ operand (F⍤y, y a value not a function) suspended on the )SI
      ⍝ used to throw SYNTAX ERROR half-way through )SAVE
      ⍝ (DerivedFunction::get_RO() calling Token::get_function()
      ⍝ unconditionally), truncating whatever workspace file already
      ⍝ existed under that name. )SAVE now encodes a value-bound
      ⍝ operand as a "*-vid" reference instead of crashing, and writes
      ⍝ to a temporary file renamed onto the target only on success, so
      ⍝ a still-imperfect save/reload of this documented-unsupported
      ⍝ )SI state (see the WARNING, CERR-only and not checked here)
      ⍝ can no longer destroy a good file.
      ⍝
      )CLEAR
CLEAR WS

      )DROP dws29.xml
³

      Z←(⌽⍤1⊢1 2)÷0
DOMAIN ERROR
      Z←(⌽⍤1⊢1 2)÷0
        ^        ^

      )WSID dws29
WAS CLEAR WS

      )SAVE
20⁰-⁰-⁰  ⁰:⁰:⁰ (GMT⁵⁰)  dws29

      )CLEAR
CLEAR WS

      )LOAD dws29.xml
SAVED 20⁰-⁰-⁰ ⁰:⁰:⁰ (GMT⁵⁰)

      )DROP dws29.xml
³

      ⍝ regression (Bugs28 #99): )LOAD of a workspace whose <SI-entry
      ⍝ level="..."> attribute disagrees with the entry's actual
      ⍝ position in the )SI stack (e.g. a hand-edited or otherwise
      ⍝ corrupt file) used to hit a raw Assert(lev == level) in
      ⍝ XML_Loading_Archive::read_SI_entry(), taking down the whole
      ⍝ session with a C++ assertion backtrace. Thrown as DOMAIN_ERROR
      ⍝ instead -- and, per explicit direction (stricter than the
      ⍝ report's own "want" of a partial-recovery diagnostic), no
      ⍝ longer caught inside read_StateIndicator() at all: the whole
      ⍝ )LOAD is refused instead of silently accepting a workspace with
      ⍝ a partially-reconstructed )SI. Workspace::load_WS() clears the
      ⍝ workspace back out (symbols/functions are read before the
      ⍝ trailing <StateIndicator>, so F below is already defined by the
      ⍝ time the corrupt entry is reached) and reports failure, so F is
      ⍝ gone and )SI is empty afterward, exactly as if the )LOAD had
      ⍝ never been attempted.
      ⍝
      )CLEAR
CLEAR WS

      )WSID silevel_test
WAS CLEAR WS

      ⎕FX 'Z←F B' 'Z←1÷B'
F

      F 0
DOMAIN ERROR
F[1]  Z←1÷B
        ^^

      )SAVE silevel_test
20⁰-⁰-⁰  ⁰:⁰:⁰ (GMT⁵⁰) 

      data ← ⎕FIO[26] 'testcases/libroot/workspaces/silevel_test.xml'
      needle ← '<SI-entry level="1"'
      pos ← (needle ⍷ data) ⍳ 1
      replacement ← '<SI-entry level="5"'
      new_data ← ((pos-1)↑data) , replacement , (((pos-1)+≢needle)↓data)
      Handle ← 'w' ⎕FIO[3] 'testcases/libroot/workspaces/silevel_test.xml'
      Wcount ← (⎕UCS new_data) ⎕FIO[7] Handle

      ⎕FIO[4] Handle
0

      ⍝ note: the checksum-mismatch WARNING (from the raw ⎕FIO edit
      ⍝ above) goes to plain CERR, like the other WARNINGs in this
      ⍝ file, and is not part of the reference comparison. The
      ⍝ "DOMAIN ERROR+ / F 0" pair below is the level=0 entry's own
      ⍝ restoration display, which happens (as it would for any
      ⍝ genuinely suspended function) before the corrupt level=1 entry
      ⍝ is even reached; the )LOAD is still refused as a whole once it
      ⍝ is.
      ⍝
      )LOAD silevel_test.xml
DOMAIN ERROR+
      F 0
      ^
)LOAD silevel_test.xml failed: DOMAIN ERROR
      )SI
      ⎕NC 'F'
0

      )DROP silevel_test.xml
³

      ⍝ regression (plan.txt, 2026-09-07): )COPY of a workspace whose
      ⍝ file has a corrupted vid="..." for one variable (e.g. hand-
      ⍝ edited) used to hit a raw Assert() deep inside
      ⍝ XML_Loading_Archive::read_Variable() and propagate uncaught out
      ⍝ of Workspace::copy_WS() -- unlike )LOAD, )COPY mutates the
      ⍝ *live* workspace's Symbols one <Symbol> at a time with no
      ⍝ CLEAR WS to fall back to, so any symbols already copied before
      ⍝ the corrupt one (CPA below) stayed overwritten while CPB never
      ⍝ got a value at all, silently mixing old and new bindings.
      ⍝ Workspace::copy_WS() now catches the exception, and
      ⍝ Archive.cc's copy_snapshot_symbol()/copy_restore_snapshots()
      ⍝ restore every Symbol already touched by this )COPY, so CPA and
      ⍝ CPB below end up exactly as they were before the )COPY was
      ⍝ attempted, not the file's 111/222 or a half-copied mix.
      ⍝
      )CLEAR
CLEAR WS

      )WSID copy_test
WAS CLEAR WS

      CPA←111
      CPB←222
      )SAVE copy_test
20⁰-⁰-⁰  ⁰:⁰:⁰ (GMT⁵⁰) 

      data ← ⎕FIO[26] 'testcases/libroot/workspaces/copy_test.xml'
      posB ← ('"CPB"' ⍷ data) ⍳ 1
      needleOpen ← 'vid="'
      relOpen ← (needleOpen ⍷ (posB ↓ data)) ⍳ 1
      posOpen ← posB + relOpen
      digitStart ← posOpen + ≢needleOpen
      afterDigits ← digitStart ↓ data
      relQuote ← ('"' ⍷ afterDigits) ⍳ 1
      dropCount ← digitStart + relQuote - 1
      new_data ← ((digitStart - 1) ↑ data) , '99999' , (dropCount ↓ data)
      Handle ← 'w' ⎕FIO[3] 'testcases/libroot/workspaces/copy_test.xml'
      Wcount ← (⎕UCS new_data) ⎕FIO[7] Handle

      ⎕FIO[4] Handle
0

      ⍝ note: the checksum-mismatch WARNING and the Assert() backtrace
      ⍝ (from the raw ⎕FIO edit above) go to plain CERR, like the other
      ⍝ WARNINGs in this file, and are not part of the reference
      ⍝ comparison -- verify the restore behavior instead: CPA and CPB
      ⍝ must still be 999/888 (their pre-)COPY values) afterward, and
      ⍝ still ⎕NC 2 (ordinary variables), proving the )COPY was cleanly
      ⍝ undone rather than leaving CPA already-overwritten (111) or CPB
      ⍝ half-defined.
      ⍝
      )CLEAR
CLEAR WS

      CPA←999
      CPB←888
      )COPY 0 copy_test
      ⎕NC 'CPA' 'CPB'
2 2

      CPA
999

      CPB
888

      )DROP copy_test.xml
³

